1. Invalid node type in originNode causing ClassCastException inside nodeToString.
2. Invalid node type in data map value causing ClassCastException.
3. Data map contains null key (via reflection) causing NullPointerException when entry.getKey() used in origin.equals(entry.getKey()).
4. Data map contains null value causing NullPointerException inside nodeToString.
5. withReadLock supplier throws RuntimeException (e.g., we simulate by subclassing Zone and overriding withReadLock to throw). But we can't modify method. Could use reflection to set lock to null? Not.

Probably 3-4 are plausible.

